lines+=['', '**Why it fails.** Each habit family has a cap of 1.5 evidence units; the calibrated threshold is 3.637338348115496. Two saturated habit families can provide at most 3 units, so ordinary habit-only posts effectively need at least three families. Length adjustment, bundling and strongly shrunk dictionary habits leave far fewer obvious slop posts over the boundary. The dictionaries add no target/fresh flags in this frozen model; their zero-human-hit gun promotion generalizes poorly to the LinkedIn holdout. Removing dictionary guns drops LinkedIn holdout FP from 38 to 5. These observations are audit findings, not permission to retune on the holdout.','', '**Threshold and uncertainty.** The post-level one-sided 95% Clopper–Pearson requirement on the 8,189-row LinkedIn veto half permits at most **3 hits**. V2 has 3, with upper bound **0.0946563%**, below 0.1%. The 9,743-row independent LinkedIn holdout has 38 flags; its upper bound is '+f"{100*a['linkedinHoldout']['final']['human']['upper95at40']:.4f}%"+'. Thus the threshold does not establish the proposed 0.1% bound on new LinkedIn posts.','', 'Polished-light was split by original id, keeping both model variants together: 80 fitting rows/40 originals and 80 audit rows/40 originals. Both halves have zero v2 flags. Even zero out of 80 gives an upper bound of **3.6754%**, so the requested ≤2% statistical bound cannot be established without more independent controls. Good-AI none is 0/77; its corresponding upper bound is '+f"{100*a['effortful']['final']['smell']['none']['upper95at40']:.4f}%"+'. Multiple posts/variants share authors or prompts, so the post-level CP calculation assumes more independence than these corpora fully provide. Cluster bootstrap intervals and group counts are retained in audit.json.','', '**Data boundaries and one-shot evidence.** Round 2 was snapshotted before any changes in `data/eval/raw/v2/engine-r2`. Its measured target/fresh/human counts reproduce the owner’s shipped baseline. Hash: `'+frozen['round2Hash']+'`. Frozen v2 hash: `'+frozen['engineHash']+'`. Baseline/final input receipts are identical. Each ran once, protected by ignored lock receipts. Final sets, fresh prompts and all 210 effortful-prompt posts were first accessed for this final comparison; none fitted weights, base rates or the threshold.','', 'Only target tune (290 rows, obvious=1, some=.5), RAID human train (7,166 windows), permissive humans (267 windows) and polished fitting half supplied the objective. Entire polished original groups were excluded from RAID fitting. Human base rates use RAID train and permissive humans only; exact Google Books 2000–2019 unigram rates supersede pooled rates for 2,777 dictionary entries. Gamma smoothing uses .5 pseudo-count; post predicates use three length buckets. Negative objective mass is 8× target mass; polished fitting examples receive 5× their corresponding negative weight. Length reweighting uses target-tune lengths only.','', 'LinkedIn veto and the initial 300 formatted Wayback controls supplied entry-level gun checks and threshold validation only. They never estimated base rates or logistic coefficients. Wayback grew to **410** before the locked evaluations; the additional 110 rows were final-only, and both engines scored exactly the same 410. Synthetic human/mixed/context controls (56) demoted individual false guns, including AI-engineering prose, ordinary Markdown headings and a human booking offer.','', '**Architecture and learning.** Counts survive example protection, lexical overlap, list/CTA/cadence bundling, and length expectation before `phi=max(0,log1p(c)-log1p(m))`. Family evidence is `C*(1-exp(-sum(w*phi)/C))`. Vocabulary cannot supply a gate witness. Eligible posts require one validated gun or at least two habit families; style alone cannot permit Shame. The public synchronous `analyzePost` and `SlopReport` shapes and signal labels remain intact. Labels can move to the winning dictionary rule when duplicate wording is bundled.','', 'The false-positive-weighted capped logistic MAP fit is nonnegative and shrinks first-party coefficients toward round-2 priors. Dictionary habits/vocabulary have a family/source multiplier times their curated prior plus a heavily penalized entry deviation. Guns keep individual coefficients. Two predeclared shrinkage settings (1 and 4) used five prompt/original-group folds; 4 was selected in the final fit. L-BFGS-B converged. The fitted intercept is an offline optimization parameter, not an AI probability in the badge. Individual validated-gun lower bounds were projected after threshold selection so a gun reaches 40 alone through 600 words; these guns have zero calibration-negative hits, so the projection cannot change veto FP. Explicit historical fingerprints keep the 80 floor and eight-word action guard.','', '**Families and weights.** Every habit family below uses cap **1.5** (0.4124× threshold); each validated gun uses its own cap **12** and coefficient. Exact per-entry coefficients, priors, base rates, tiers, corpus hit counts and shipping decisions are in entry-table.json; optimized family/source multipliers are in fit.json; projected lower bounds are in gun-constraint.json.','', '| Family/source multiplier | Learned value |','|---|---:|']
