lines+=['', '200 distinct 300-word development excerpts, 100 human/100 chat, five timed calls each after warmup; five fresh native-TypeScript Node processes for cold measurements. The latest MVP mean-time budget (<1 ms) passes. The original strict worst-call <1 ms and creation <30 ms targets remain **unmet** (1.062 and 44.159 ms). Engine creation after the immutable singleton is prepared is near zero; the table/guard/regex initialization cost belongs to the first call and is included above. Native Node module loading includes TypeScript resolution/stripping, so it is not a browser claim.','', 'The withdrawn byte-size gate is informational only. An earlier isolated plain `pnpm build` measured linkedin.js at **940,820 bytes**, before the final score-preserving guard/type fixes; it was not rebuilt after the parent instructed no more builds. No release was installed. Cold module evaluation plus the first score is ~184 ms in Node, so startup still needs parent-owned integration work. A dedicated worker can load and warm the pure engine once, receive post ids/text, and return reports while the adapter/UI remain on the main thread. That changes the content-script scheduling boundary; worker wiring was explicitly left outside this task and is not implemented here.','', '**Test updates and their reasons.**','', '| Tests | Reason |','|---|---|','| score.test.ts | Replace old exponential/editorial point sums and hard category caps with exposure, smooth caps, actual displayed-point sums and gate assertions; retain contributor validation. |','| evidence.test.ts | Length can reduce sparse tell points and protected examples can increase exposure; preserve exact protected spans and duplicate-occurrence assertions. |','| artifacts.test.ts | Placeholder signal weights now use displayed index points rather than old 4–6 editorial points; all ≥80 fingerprint and human nondecisive guards remain. |','| packs.test.ts | Add the dictionary pack; ordinary habits may have small visible scores; accept the winning bundled dictionary span and test the same no-accusation boundary. |','| pasted-output.test.ts | Accept the winning slot span, remove the obsolete family bonus, check displayed-point arithmetic. |','| calibration.test.ts | Generic AI authorship is report-only under the owner’s definition; explicit artifacts still must reach ≥80; human negatives remain below 40. |','| recall.test.ts | Bundle duplicate list descriptions and accept calibrated scores; the synthetic cache explainer now correctly records the measured below-threshold result instead of demanding its historical 60/40 band. Other actionable examples/frozen artifacts remain required. |','| regex-regressions.test.ts | The raw matcher must retain the later construction, while extreme-length exposure may hide its φ=0 signal. |','| scorecard.test.ts | Add boundary continuity, exposure, vocabulary/gate isolation, bundles and tell-removal regressions. |','| inflate.test.ts | Decode independent stored/fixed/dynamic zlib streams and reject damaged payloads. |','', '**Risks and handoff.** Keep round 2 as the installed scorer. V2 fails target recall and does not confirm the desired held-out 0.1% human tail. Rare in these auxiliary corpora is not equivalent to a visible low-quality artifact; dictionary gun false alarms show this failure. High caps are not the only issue: template/domain coverage, correlated prompts/authors and all-positive prior retention limit the fit. Good-AI none stays protected on this one audit, but 77 examples cannot establish a 2% confidence bound. Startup/first-call blocking and the strict tail-latency/creation targets need separate engineering. This audit is closed: any future accuracy revision requires a new confirmatory split; do not hill-climb against these final results.','', 'All text-bearing inputs, spans, predictions, raw features and snapshots stay under ignored data/eval/raw/v2. Source changes are limited to the engine; test changes are limited to engine tests. No UI, adapter, entrypoint, public asset, INTENTIONS or HANDOFF changes, no network, browsers, commits, or installation. The owner-authorized isolated build directory was removed. No task process remains after final checks.']
